  "findings": [
    "cyclicPred and cyclicSucc compute predecessor/successor in ZMod n before taking a bounded Fin value. Cast, ordinary-position, zero-wrap and last-wrap equations verify this actual cyclic convention. The source n>=3 premise derives that both neighbors differ from s; no n>=4 or interior-s premise is substituted.",
    "For an interval starting at A with right beyond B, strict collapsed bounds and leaf count1 force the right collapsed value to be s+1. Its own Fin bound excludes wrap here. The ending-B case similarly forces the left value to s\u22121 with s>0. Substituting those actual neighbors in the proposed ordinary table makes the respective factor zero for every t and b0, including zero b0 values. These are table-value/factor statements, not yet the full endpoint transform identity.",
    "The full child interval cannot be [A,B] for n>=3, and its collapsed endpoints are exactly0 and n\u22121. Endpoint extensionality therefore identifies the full core interval, without assuming any composition or amplitude correspondence.",
    "boundaryIndex transports the literal cyclic predecessor/successor to actual physical labels j\u22121/j+1 when s is the proved softRootPosition. Combining this with the frozen geometric data identifies formal etaMinus/etaPlus with both physical attachment signs. No freely chosen root correspondence or neighbor-value premise remains in this bridge.",
    "Injectivity of the root-to-position map and the earlier incoming/return values give exact first iff incoming and last iff return. The complementary strict position interval is exactly the remaining roots. The full-interval cases match the source starting, ending and strictly spanning alternatives; hn3 ensures endpoint cases have the required strict exterior endpoint.",
    "First45759 failed only on an unreduced numeric Fin endpoint, a lambda application in an equality used for rewriting, and substitution removing the variable name needed by a final proof. The repaired proof normalizes those terms and chooses explicit substitution direction. All24 public signatures are unchanged; exact failed drafts/log and repair bindings are preserved. Second36793 exited0 with24 standard-only traces and16 exact embedded bodies."
  ],
  "limits": "This bridges formal cyclic eta data, one-leaf endpoint table factors and full-root interval placements. It does not prove the nonavoiding weighted transform, full ordinary recurrence/uniqueness, final root multiplier, A-soft or C-soft. No source row is accepted."
